// Four fields are hardware-writable, so the mirror can legitimately
// disagree with the DUT and a check would be a false failure rather
// than a detection. Each one is masked here exactly where
// tb/env/axi_scoreboard.sv masks it, so the two models make the same
// claim about what is knowable at transaction level:
//
//   STATUS.busy      cycle-level     scoreboard mask 32'hFFFF_FFFE
//   STATUS.error     hw-written on every completed transaction
//   COUNTER.count    free-running    scoreboard checks only the
//                                    cleared-and-frozen state
//   INT_STATUS[3]    follows COUNTER scoreboard mask 32'hFFFF_FFF7
//
// The INT_STATUS bits that the environment CAN predict keep their
// comparison, because that comparison is what catches an INT_STATUS
// implemented as plain RW (spec section 9, BUG-004).
//
// NOT independently compilable -- see tb/agent/axi_transaction.sv.
